WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:03.150
Marvel movies are for kids… right?

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:08.990
Well, based on the jump scares and scary imagery,
"Doctor Strange 2" is apparently for making

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.559
kids cry.

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:15.629
Here are all the things only adults noticed
in the surprisingly frightening "Doctor Strange

00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:17.150
in the Multiverse of Madness."

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.060
The one thing that was abundantly clear about
America Chavez in "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.970
of Madness" was that she had seen a lot.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:31.050
Having traveled across the Multiverse, she
had visited 72 universes before landing on

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.380
Earth-616.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:38.390
However, there was one superhero she had failed
to encounter or even know anything about during

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.789
her adventures: Spider-Man.

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:45.010
While most people might point out that it's
because of Doctor Strange's spell at the end

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:49.719
of "Spider-Man: No Way Home," that's not an
entirely correct assumption.

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:54.180
Strange's spell made everyone forget that
Peter Parker existed, not Spidey.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.990
Even Happy Hogan confirmed to Pete that he
knew Aunt May through Spider-Man at her gravesite.

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:04.340
Taking into account the three Spider-Men that
appeared in "No Way Home," plus all the others

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:09.770
introduced in "Into the Spider-Verse," what
are the odds that America only visited universes

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:13.270
without any spider-themed heroes or variants?

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.610
No Miles Morales?

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.110
No Miguel O'Hara?

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.110
No Spider-Gwen?

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.820
Hmm ... This is starting to smell a whole
lot like a gigantic plot hole.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:27.510
Wanda Maximoff experienced a heartbreaking
and life-changing moment when she removed

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:32.230
the Mind Stone from Vision's head, which was
a vital part of keeping him alive.

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:37.500
Then, she had to suffer the pain and loss
all over again, as Thanos reversed time and

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.820
destroyed the android once more for good measure.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.600
These events can change someone – and in
Wanda's case, they had a big effect, as we

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.500
all saw in "WandaVision."

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.460
Her grieving process was, to say the least,
ethically questionable.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:55.980
"If you won't let us go, just let us die."

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:01.310
While we cannot condone Wanda's actions or
methods, her former teammates hardly made

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:04.840
any effort to provide her comfort during her
period of grief.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:10.759
Sure, everyone experienced their own losses
after Thanos' snap and had a lot to deal with,

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:15.600
but no one attempted to even be a shoulder
to cry on for Wanda, even knowing that she'd

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.900
lost her brother, Pietro, and then the love
of her life.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.870
In all likelihood, Wanda might have pushed
them away, but at least she would have known

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.540
they cared about her.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.780
Ultimately, she was alone and this led her
to the Darkhold and the path of trying to

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.510
create a family to deal with her trauma.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.510
With friends like the Avengers, who needs
enemies, right?

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:40.610
"And now… it's time for some good news."

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:44.860
Undoubtedly, one of the hottest cameos of
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:51.900
was the appearance of John Krasinski as the
Reed Richards, aka Mister Fantastic, of Earth-838.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.300
While social media might have spoiled the
big reveal because Film Twitter cannot contain

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:01.360
itself with secrets, it was still an exciting
moment, as it announced the official arrival

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.960
of the Fantastic Four in the MCU.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.980
The rest of Marvel's First Family didn't show
up, but it was more than enough to lay a solid

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.320
foundation for the impending film.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:16.140
With the confirmation that the Fantastic Four
exists within the multiverse, it leaves one

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:21.930
major question here: Why didn't the Earth-616
version of the team try to stop Thanos with

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:22.970
the Avengers?

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:28.480
Yes, Krasinski's Mister Fantastic was from
a different universe, but there must be other

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.940
versions of the Fantastic Four sprinkled throughout
the Multiverse.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.980
Are we meant to believe that Reed Richards
— one of the world's greatest minds — didn't

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.130
have anything to add and chose to stay at
home in the Baxter Building while the rest

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.210
of Earth's heroes battled Thanos' evil forces?

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:46.280
They must've been busy with something interesting.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.490
Maybe we'll get some answers in the upcoming
movie.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:54.390
Fox's X-Men series ended quietly with the
release of The New Mutants, preceded by the

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.069
purchase of 20th Century Fox by Disney.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:01.970
But long before that purchase, the "canon"
of the X-Men movies had become hopelessly

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.010
confusing.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.240
That timeline has undergone more revamps and
reimaginings than "Extreme Makeover: Home

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.240
Edition."

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:13.020
Without a doubt, the MCU will try to remedy
this situation with the Children of the Atom

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:19.600
becoming a part of the greater Marvel Universe,
and the first step was introducing the Earth-838

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:23.740
version of Patrick Stewart's Professor Charles
Xavier in "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.080
of Madness."

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:30.090
While Stewart's Professor X was from Fox's
X-Verse, there are a few hints that he may

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:34.090
be the mutant from another popular incarnation
of the X-Men.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:38.940
When Professor X appeared in the film, he
glided onto the screen in the recognizable

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.370
yellow hover chair from "X-Men: The Animated
Series."

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:47.040
Additionally, he wore a green top to match
the character's design from the cartoon.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:52.130
However, the biggest a-ha moment was when
a hint of the classic theme song from the

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.500
animated show played in the background.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.910
Of course this could be a homage or merely
fan service for long-time supporters of the

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:04.360
mutant superheroes, but wouldn't it be a novel
idea if "X-Men: The Animated Series" ends

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.620
up being the backstory of the MCU's X-Men?

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:13.220
With the animated show returning with the
upcoming sequel series "X-Men '97" on Disney+,

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.760
don't bet against it.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:19.380
The fact that the title of the film includes
"Multiverse of Madness" is a good indication

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:22.169
that not everything was meant to make sense
here.

00:05:22.169 --> 00:05:26.040
However, there was one glaring issue that
cannot be overlooked.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:30.210
Remember "Spider-Man: No Way Home" and how
it brought all the Peter Parkers together?

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:35.060
While it was fun to hear MJ and Ned call Peter
and for all of them to respond at the same

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:39.180
time, it was evident that all three Peters
looked different and were distinguishable

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.180
from each other.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.770
"This is Peter Parker, this is Peter Parker,
Spider-Man, Spider-Man, they're mes from other universes."

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.010
"Oh, no."

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:51.090
So why did the variants of Stephen Strange,
Christine Palmer, and Wanda Maximoff all look

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.800
the same in the Multiverse?

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:57.610
Apart from a different haircut or some slightly
different attire, they all looked identical.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:02.820
It was easy to spot who they were, and the
shared features made them instantly recognizable

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.850
to people from other universes.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:09.340
Using this logic, all three of the Spider-Men
should have looked like Tom Holland's version

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.690
of the character.

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:15.090
Naturally, this new logic could be a result
of Doctor Strange's spells having adverse

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:20.380
effects on the Multiverse, but it still seemed
peculiar how America Chavez, who had been

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:24.570
traversing the universes for some time, didn't
mention anything about it.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:30.820
In Earth-616, Iron Man sacrificed himself
to end Thanos' reign of terror.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:35.820
In "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,"
it was shown how the Illuminati also brought

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:38.400
down the Mad Titan in their own universe.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:43.480
Connecting the dots, this points to one significant
conclusion: There are multiple versions of

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:48.008
Thanos throughout the Multiverse and they're
all likely hungry for power.

00:06:48.856 --> 00:06:52.240
"Impossible."

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.990
As portals have been opened and people have
zipped in and out of the different universes,

00:06:56.990 --> 00:07:00.930
what are the odds that another Thanos hasn't
slipped through the cracks as well?

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:06.900
His brother Eros, aka Starfox, was introduced
in the post-credits scene of "Eternals;" a

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:12.580
powerful figure like him will need a formidable
foe, and who is more formidable than his brother,

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:13.580
the Mad Titan?

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:19.430
A villain as big and monumental as Thanos
doesn't just go away quietly after one rumble.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:23.990
It's not outside the realm of possibility
that some version of him may be laying low

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:28.990
and licking his wounds, as he plots his revenge
on Earth's Mightiest Heroes and prepares to

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.250
strike once again.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:36.020
Previous MCU films have made it clear that
Wanda Maximoff is a powerful character; you

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:40.070
may recall that she appeared capable of defeating
Thanos almost single-handedly.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:45.449
However, as the Scarlet Witch in "Doctor Strange
in the Multiverse of Madness," she showed

00:07:45.449 --> 00:07:50.539
off just how OP she really was.

00:07:50.539 --> 00:07:56.800
Not only did she wipe out Captain Carter,
Captain Marvel, Reed Richards, and Black Bolt

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:02.610
on her own, but she also wiped out the army
of Kamar-Taj without breaking a sweat.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:07.009
Forget about great power and great responsibility,
because when someone holds the potential to

00:08:07.009 --> 00:08:12.100
get into people's heads and snap them like
they're twigs, it's best to put pride aside

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.200
and call in the heavy guns for help.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.110
For some reason, though, Doctor Strange didn't
do that.

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:22.010
He knew that Scarlet Witch was heading to
Kamar-Taj to collect America Chavez, and she

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:24.800
had already told him her demands beforehand.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:30.490
Yet, instead of phoning up the Avengers and
asking for some superpowered backup, he decided

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:34.409
to rely on magic students as the frontline
of defense.

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:38.789
Perhaps Strange underestimated his former
colleague, but he could have at least called

00:08:38.789 --> 00:08:44.019
up Jimmy Woo and Darcy Lewis to find out how
much damage the Scarlet Witch had caused at Westview.

00:08:44.019 --> 00:08:49.306
Maybe then he wouldn't have been so reluctant
to seek out major assistance in the first place.

00:08:49.822 --> 00:08:54.699
When Doctor Strange tried to reason with Scarlet
Witch about the severe consequences of messing

00:08:54.699 --> 00:08:59.410
with the Multiverse, she turned the tables
and pointed out how it was deemed acceptable

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:00.519
when he did the same.

00:09:00.519 --> 00:09:06.740
"You break the rules and become a hero; I
do it and I become the enemy."

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:09.819
She says it's not fair, and she's not wrong.

00:09:09.819 --> 00:09:14.380
While there was an element of whataboutism
in her response, she raised a valid point

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:16.740
about Strange's double standards.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:21.740
In "Spider-Man: No Way Home," Wong warned
him about what would happen, but Strange didn't

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.080
heed his warnings.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:28.619
Instead, he opened the world to possible new
threats because of a request from Spider-Man.

00:09:28.619 --> 00:09:34.399
While it was undoubtedly sad that Spidey's
true identity was exposed to the world, Strange

00:09:34.399 --> 00:09:39.129
was prepared to risk the safety of the entire
universe to reverse a single event.

00:09:39.129 --> 00:09:41.839
Surely, there were other solutions here.

00:09:41.839 --> 00:09:45.300
Even if it meant that Peter Parker would have
to hide out for a period of time until they

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:46.499
figured it out.

00:09:46.499 --> 00:09:51.519
Yet, the first port of call here was magic
— the kind that creates seismic rifts in

00:09:51.519 --> 00:09:52.790
the universe.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:57.439
While Scarlet Witch wasn't right in wanting
to sacrifice a person for her own delusion

00:09:57.439 --> 00:10:02.579
of personal happiness, neither was Strange,
who was prepared to risk an entire world for

00:10:02.579 --> 00:10:03.579
one person.

00:10:04.579 --> 00:10:09.130
From what we have seen in the MCU, Doctor
Strange has never been what one would call

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.379
a "people person."

00:10:10.379 --> 00:10:14.379
He can come across as prickly, condescending,
and sometimes even cruel.

00:10:14.379 --> 00:10:18.970
"This isn't the end; there are other things
that can give your life meaning."

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.119
"Like what – like you?"

00:10:21.119 --> 00:10:26.429
However, he displayed a lot of initial disrespect
to Wong in "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse

00:10:26.429 --> 00:10:27.529
of Madness."

00:10:27.529 --> 00:10:31.999
When approaching the Sorcerer Supreme, there
were certain formalities that needed to be

00:10:31.999 --> 00:10:34.999
adhered to, such as bowing before him.

00:10:34.999 --> 00:10:40.290
For Strange, he didn't do this for the better
part of the film, only doing so in the end.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:45.579
It was surprising to see Strange behave this
way, since Wong had not only been a friend,

00:10:45.579 --> 00:10:49.240
but also the person who assisted him in studying
the Mystic Arts.

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:53.439
He had a wealth of knowledge and even knew
important concepts about the Multiverse that

00:10:53.439 --> 00:10:55.589
Strange had no idea about.

00:10:55.589 --> 00:11:00.190
Much like "Spider-Man: No Way Home," Strange
didn't listen to Wong when he really should

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:01.190
have.

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:04.630
Hopefully, his change in demeanor at the end
of "Multiverse of Madness" signified that

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:10.013
he would be taking Wong and his position as
the Sorcerer Supreme much more seriously in

00:11:10.013 --> 00:11:11.517
the future.

00:11:13.319 --> 00:11:16.519
"Oh, that's funny."

00:11:17.519 --> 00:11:21.829
Out of all the characters from the previous
Marvel films and TV shows, who would have

00:11:21.829 --> 00:11:26.470
put money on an Inhuman showing up in "Doctor
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness"?

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:33.839
Lest we forget, the "Inhumans" TV show holds
an 11% critical approval rating and 44% audience

00:11:33.839 --> 00:11:35.709
score on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:11:35.709 --> 00:11:39.860
After all the ridicule and bad press, one
would imagine that Kevin Feige would have

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:44.319
sent the Inhumans into the darkest part of
the Multiverse, never to be seen again.

00:11:44.319 --> 00:11:48.910
Yet, Anson Mount returned as Black Bolt in
Sam Raimi's film.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:54.040
This time, however, he was kitted out in a
comic book-accurate outfit and portrayed as

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:57.880
more of an omega-level threat than what was
seen in the series.

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:01.869
Like his comic book counterpart, no one wanted
him to speak a word, knowing that a single

00:12:01.869 --> 00:12:04.840
whisper could decimate anyone around him.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:08.720
"Why?"

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:13.129
Equally important here, "Doctor Strange in
the Multiverse of Madness" proved that there

00:12:13.129 --> 00:12:17.179
could be life and a future for the Inhumans
in the MCU.

00:12:17.179 --> 00:12:21.059
Not that team, necessarily, but the Inhumans
in general.

00:12:21.059 --> 00:12:24.999
They might have had a rough time on the ABC
show, but they could still play an important

00:12:24.999 --> 00:12:27.439
part in Marvel movies going forward.

00:12:27.439 --> 00:12:32.815
Maybe Mount may return as Black Bolt for a
third time, ensuring that Vin Diesel's long-standing

00:12:32.815 --> 00:12:36.332
dream of playing the silent superhero never
happens.

